WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.994
- You kind of have to
just dive into everyday

00:00:01.994 --> 00:00:04.447
like this is the last
time I'm going to do this.

00:00:04.447 --> 00:00:06.351
I think that's how you become the best.

00:00:06.351 --> 00:00:08.914
I just work so hard to prove
that my talent was enough

00:00:08.914 --> 00:00:11.491
that I didn't have to fit
in to this box and this mold

00:00:11.491 --> 00:00:13.549
of what everyone thinks of which is.

00:00:13.549 --> 00:00:17.732
You can do anything you want
even if you're being told

00:00:17.732 --> 00:00:18.617
negative things.

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:22.147
Just to stay strong and find motivation.

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:24.030
- She's an American ballet dancer.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.421
She rose to stardom
despite not starting ballet

00:00:27.421 --> 00:00:29.034
until the age of 13.

00:00:29.034 --> 00:00:31.252
In addition to her dance
career she's become a public

00:00:31.252 --> 00:00:33.205
speaker and stage performer.

00:00:33.205 --> 00:00:35.513
She's Misty Copeland and
here's my take on her

00:00:35.513 --> 00:00:37.015
top ten rules of success.

00:00:37.015 --> 00:00:38.823
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:38.823 --> 00:00:41.055
and I'd love to know which
ones you guys like the best.

00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:42.272
And as always as you're watching

00:00:42.272 --> 00:00:44.993
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:44.993 --> 00:00:46.351
please leave it in the comments below.

00:00:46.351 --> 00:00:47.201
Put quotes around it

00:00:47.201 --> 00:00:49.253
so other people could be inspired as well.

00:00:49.253 --> 00:00:50.496
And when you write it down

00:00:50.496 --> 00:00:53.282
it's much more likely to
stick with you as well.

00:00:53.282 --> 00:00:54.115
Enjoy.

00:00:57.131 --> 00:01:00.048
(futuristic music)

00:01:07.181 --> 00:01:09.764
(upbeat music)

00:03:00.154 --> 00:03:03.210
- I haven't had the typical
path of most dancers

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:06.466
especially as a professional dancer.

00:03:06.466 --> 00:03:10.398
To be in the corps de
ballet and to be a soloist

00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:12.243
for as long as I was

00:03:12.243 --> 00:03:15.854
and to then get my first big
break doing a principal role,

00:03:15.854 --> 00:03:17.851
that's not typical.

00:03:17.851 --> 00:03:22.849
Usually if that doesn't
happen early on in your career

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:25.821
that path is kind of shut
down for you to ever become

00:03:25.821 --> 00:03:27.191
a principal dancer.

00:03:27.191 --> 00:03:32.175
So I knew that when Alexei
Ratmansky, the choreographer,

00:03:32.175 --> 00:03:34.679
choreographer and residence
at ABT and the choreographer

00:03:34.679 --> 00:03:35.679
of Firebird.

00:03:37.086 --> 00:03:38.603
When he gave me the opportunity

00:03:38.603 --> 00:03:43.064
to learn the role I knew
that this was kind of my last

00:03:43.064 --> 00:03:45.121
opportunity to prove

00:03:45.121 --> 00:03:46.719
at 29 years old

00:03:46.719 --> 00:03:49.250
that I'm capable of still being able

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.141
to develop into an artist that can

00:03:52.141 --> 00:03:54.265
carry an entire company on my shoulders

00:03:54.265 --> 00:03:55.937
as a principal dancer.

00:03:55.937 --> 00:03:59.626
So I just kind of went
into it like head-first

00:03:59.626 --> 00:04:02.126
and worked so incredibly hard,

00:04:03.005 --> 00:04:04.572
didn't take any days off

00:04:04.572 --> 00:04:06.697
which I wouldn't recommend to anyone.

00:04:06.697 --> 00:04:11.375
And during that process of
having Firebird created for me

00:04:11.375 --> 00:04:14.022
I developed six stress
fractures in my tibia.

00:04:14.022 --> 00:04:16.367
- Let's say that again, six fractures.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:17.200
- Yes.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.268
- In your tibia that you
still danced on and did that

00:04:21.268 --> 00:04:22.764
the night of the performance.

00:04:22.764 --> 00:04:25.260
- Yeah, I didn't know the
severity of the injury

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.744
and I think that was kind of
a way of protecting myself

00:04:27.744 --> 00:04:31.912
that I didn't want to know
how badly I was injured,

00:04:31.912 --> 00:04:34.270
and so I pushed through
as long as I could.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.934
I knew that I had to get a
couple of shows under my belt

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.885
and prove that I was capable.

00:04:38.885 --> 00:04:41.300
- You talk about this
confidence, this perseverance,

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.926
you didn't want to let people down,

00:04:42.926 --> 00:04:46.121
but still most of us feel that way,

00:04:46.121 --> 00:04:49.932
but may not have the whatever it takes

00:04:49.932 --> 00:04:51.432
to get through it.

00:04:53.473 --> 00:04:56.350
- I think a lot of it is
being African American

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.879
and having the struggles and
the experiences that I've had

00:04:58.879 --> 00:05:01.629
and seeing all of the people that

00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:06.604
seeing me on the stage,
how it's affected them.

00:05:06.604 --> 00:05:09.843
That's what kept me going on those days

00:05:09.843 --> 00:05:12.003
when I couldn't physically walk,

00:05:12.003 --> 00:05:15.238
when I had doubts and thought,

00:05:15.238 --> 00:05:16.701
why am I fighting so hard?

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.930
I might not ever be able to jump again.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.288
Why am I doing this?

00:05:20.288 --> 00:05:23.435
And it was those little brown girls.

00:05:23.435 --> 00:05:26.360
It was those girls in the
audience that were there

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.799
the night of Firebird.

00:05:28.799 --> 00:05:30.632
That made me feel that

00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:34.635
I was going to do it no matter what

00:05:34.635 --> 00:05:37.746
physical obstacles I felt I was
going to find a way around it

00:05:37.746 --> 00:05:39.829
because what was possible

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.430
for me to create

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.670
could change the future
for so many young dancers

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:49.837
and it just makes you
super-human when you feel that.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.402
- The weight of that
though, the responsibility--

00:05:53.402 --> 00:05:55.852
- But I didn't feel it
as weight it felt like

00:05:55.852 --> 00:05:58.935
this amazing support and energy from,

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.034
you know,

00:06:02.034 --> 00:06:04.219
all of these people that
are there to support me

00:06:04.219 --> 00:06:05.410
and that were watching me

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.266
because I was creating a path for them.

00:06:08.266 --> 00:06:10.526
I think that when I was younger,

00:06:10.526 --> 00:06:13.939
you get so like, antsy and
you just want the good things

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:16.737
to come and it's hard to enjoy the process

00:06:16.737 --> 00:06:19.233
and I think that's something
that I really understand

00:06:19.233 --> 00:06:20.894
and appreciate now.

00:06:20.894 --> 00:06:24.144
I mean my life is so
chaotic with just being busy

00:06:24.144 --> 00:06:25.944
all the time that I literally just take

00:06:25.944 --> 00:06:28.223
everything one step at a time.

00:06:28.223 --> 00:06:30.778
Like even when I'm on the stage,

00:06:30.778 --> 00:06:32.876
and I'm like I can't think about third act

00:06:32.876 --> 00:06:34.499
I'm in second act now
and I'm going to think

00:06:34.499 --> 00:06:36.891
about the piqué en
arabesque I'm about to do,

00:06:36.891 --> 00:06:41.372
not about the pirouettes I'm
going to do in two seconds.

00:06:41.372 --> 00:06:44.733
So it's literally just
like taking everything,

00:06:44.733 --> 00:06:47.726
you know, just pacing yourself
in one thing at a time.

00:06:47.726 --> 00:06:51.559
So when I for some reason
felt that I had this

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:56.700
small bit of confidence to
audition for the drill team

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.036
and I made sure I was
auditioning for captain not just

00:06:59.036 --> 00:07:01.761
to be apart of the team, which was not,

00:07:01.761 --> 00:07:04.125
that was not something that
I normally did in my life,

00:07:04.125 --> 00:07:06.194
like step outside of my
comfort zone and do something

00:07:06.194 --> 00:07:09.962
where I was being put
out in front of people.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:13.257
But I auditioned and they made me captain

00:07:13.257 --> 00:07:15.946
and the drill team
coach, Elizabeth Cantine,

00:07:15.946 --> 00:07:18.190
saw something in me immediately.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:22.723
She saw an ability that I
had, my body proportions,

00:07:22.723 --> 00:07:25.367
and she thought, you are a ballerina.

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:27.460
And I want to introduce
you to someone who's giving

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.442
a free ballet class at
the Boys and Girls Club

00:07:29.442 --> 00:07:31.968
that you already attend.

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:35.131
I was not at all interested in ballet

00:07:35.131 --> 00:07:38.869
but after about a week
of hiding out in the back

00:07:38.869 --> 00:07:41.903
of this ballet class on
the basketball court,

00:07:41.903 --> 00:07:44.442
the teacher, Cynthia Bradley, pulled me on

00:07:44.442 --> 00:07:49.441
and I took my first class in
socks and shorts and a t-shirt.

00:07:49.441 --> 00:07:51.612
I think that if we woke up every morning

00:07:51.612 --> 00:07:55.121
and we looked at our day or our careers

00:07:55.121 --> 00:07:57.126
as though something was going to go wrong

00:07:57.126 --> 00:07:58.739
or something could happen,

00:07:58.739 --> 00:08:01.209
we couldn't reach our fullest potential.

00:08:01.209 --> 00:08:03.254
You kind of have to
just dive into every day

00:08:03.254 --> 00:08:05.563
like this is the last
time I'm going to do this.

00:08:05.563 --> 00:08:07.343
I think that's how you become the best,

00:08:07.343 --> 00:08:10.310
that's how you become your best self.

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:11.952
You know, I don't step
on to the stage thinking,

00:08:11.952 --> 00:08:14.836
I might fall tonight, it's
like, I'm going to go for it

00:08:14.836 --> 00:08:18.084
and if I fall how am I going to recover.

00:08:18.084 --> 00:08:20.704
That's kind of the approach
that you have to have

00:08:20.704 --> 00:08:23.339
especially when you're at this level.

00:08:23.339 --> 00:08:25.501
That you can't think about,

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:26.590
you know, what if.

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.590
What if this goes wrong?

00:08:29.632 --> 00:08:31.273
Just keep striving.

00:08:31.273 --> 00:08:34.073
I think it's important to be
passionate about what you do

00:08:34.073 --> 00:08:37.356
but know that it doesn't
come without hard work.

00:08:37.356 --> 00:08:40.329
Success doesn't come without sacrifice.

00:08:40.329 --> 00:08:43.266
And it's a beautiful thing

00:08:43.266 --> 00:08:44.775
when you put all that work

00:08:44.775 --> 00:08:46.853
into what you're passionate about.

00:08:46.853 --> 00:08:51.238
You can sit back and enjoy
the fruits of your labor.

00:08:51.238 --> 00:08:54.761
You know I can't say where I will go next

00:08:54.761 --> 00:08:57.780
but I know that ballet
will take me everywhere

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:01.298
that I can imagine dreaming of going

00:09:01.298 --> 00:09:03.465
and it's pretty awesome.

00:09:03.465 --> 00:09:04.937
- And there were other issues too right,

00:09:04.937 --> 00:09:07.259
with your body type because
you're very athletic.

00:09:07.259 --> 00:09:10.417
Okay, she's so tiny sitting next to me.

00:09:10.417 --> 00:09:12.468
But you're incredibly
athletic and that also

00:09:12.468 --> 00:09:14.105
created some problems right?

00:09:14.105 --> 00:09:15.688
- Yeah, there just,

00:09:17.042 --> 00:09:19.004
I guess you can call them setbacks

00:09:19.004 --> 00:09:20.653
but I overcame them.

00:09:20.653 --> 00:09:22.812
They just continue to come.

00:09:22.812 --> 00:09:24.577
You know, once I became a professional,

00:09:24.577 --> 00:09:27.398
I, all of a sudden matured
into this curvy woman

00:09:27.398 --> 00:09:30.393
with a bust and with more
muscle and all of those things

00:09:30.393 --> 00:09:32.982
also are not thought of as a ballerina.

00:09:32.982 --> 00:09:36.070
And I just worked so hard to prove

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.149
that my talent was enough
that I didn't have to fit

00:09:38.149 --> 00:09:41.226
into this box and this mold
of what everyone thinks of

00:09:41.226 --> 00:09:46.143
which is, a white woman
with no chest and no muscle

00:09:46.143 --> 00:09:48.465
and I was everything that that wasn't.

00:09:48.465 --> 00:09:50.969
Being a Black ballerina

00:09:50.969 --> 00:09:53.052
definitely is everything.

00:09:54.175 --> 00:09:56.508
And my life and my path as a ballerina

00:09:56.508 --> 00:09:57.823
would be completely different

00:09:57.823 --> 00:10:00.087
if I wasn't an African American woman.

00:10:00.087 --> 00:10:04.635
It has provided more
obstacles than I think I knew

00:10:04.635 --> 00:10:07.898
when I discovered ballet at 13 years old.

00:10:07.898 --> 00:10:11.021
But at the same time it's made me want to

00:10:11.021 --> 00:10:12.890
persevere even more and
I think it's made me

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:15.105
a stronger person because of it.

00:10:15.105 --> 00:10:17.650
And I have so many more
obstacles to overcome

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.843
but I absolutely love classical ballet.

00:10:20.843 --> 00:10:22.928
- [Interviewer] You've
accomplished so much.

00:10:22.928 --> 00:10:25.186
At this point in your career
what is your driving force,

00:10:25.186 --> 00:10:29.168
and what is it that's keeping
you going every single day?

00:10:29.168 --> 00:10:31.443
- Well the thing is I have so much more

00:10:31.443 --> 00:10:33.183
I want to accomplish.

00:10:33.183 --> 00:10:36.016
So I think that as a ballet dancer

00:10:37.014 --> 00:10:39.791
you're constantly being
pushed to kind of stay

00:10:39.791 --> 00:10:41.407
on top of your game

00:10:41.407 --> 00:10:44.449
and with so many younger dancers

00:10:44.449 --> 00:10:46.237
that continue to come into the company

00:10:46.237 --> 00:10:48.373
it's like you have to keep up with them.

00:10:48.373 --> 00:10:52.051
I mean every generation gets better

00:10:52.051 --> 00:10:54.430
so that's constantly like pushing me

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:55.803
and I just love what I do.

00:10:55.803 --> 00:10:57.878
And I think as dancers
we're constantly striving

00:10:57.878 --> 00:11:00.908
for perfection and that's
never going to happen.

00:11:00.908 --> 00:11:03.593
So it's just going to
keep us going and going.

00:11:03.593 --> 00:11:06.403
But, you know, I have so
many new roles coming up

00:11:06.403 --> 00:11:10.641
that I'm excited about so
that's keeping me motivated.

00:11:10.641 --> 00:11:13.191
And, of course, being a principal dancer

00:11:13.191 --> 00:11:15.499
that's my number one goal.

00:11:15.499 --> 00:11:19.233
I understand the importance
of me having a voice

00:11:19.233 --> 00:11:21.555
and exposing people beyond,

00:11:21.555 --> 00:11:24.550
you know, the typical ballet
world to this art form.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:26.258
I think it saved my life,

00:11:26.258 --> 00:11:29.141
and I want to introduce it to more people

00:11:29.141 --> 00:11:31.389
and coming full-circle that's something

00:11:31.389 --> 00:11:33.432
that I'm trying to do now is to give back

00:11:33.432 --> 00:11:37.115
to those communities through
Boys and Girls Clubs,

00:11:37.115 --> 00:11:38.397
being an alum,

00:11:38.397 --> 00:11:41.890
to invite people into my
world as it's happening.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:45.700
I think it's really
amazing to have grown men

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:48.069
that have never seen
a ballet in their life

00:11:48.069 --> 00:11:52.026
look at me and see a woman
that they can relate to,

00:11:52.026 --> 00:11:54.266
someone who looks like their
sister, their daughter,

00:11:54.266 --> 00:11:57.471
their mother and to say, well
I'm going to put my child in that

00:11:57.471 --> 00:11:59.410
because they can see
themselves through you.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.254
I think it's creating a
completely different path

00:12:01.254 --> 00:12:03.726
through these people
that never saw themselves

00:12:03.726 --> 00:12:06.977
in this world and to
watch me still growing

00:12:06.977 --> 00:12:10.477
and on my path I think is really powerful.

00:12:12.504 --> 00:12:15.671
I was very open to accepting guidance,

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.364
and I think that that's
something that you really

00:12:19.364 --> 00:12:21.372
have to be vulnerable and open to

00:12:21.372 --> 00:12:23.532
or these people will just kind of pass by

00:12:23.532 --> 00:12:27.283
and they don't enter your
life when they should be.

00:12:27.283 --> 00:12:29.700
And Prince came into my life,

00:12:30.989 --> 00:12:32.749
I think I was around 27?

00:12:32.749 --> 00:12:33.724
I'm 31 now.

00:12:33.724 --> 00:12:37.791
And he thought I was extremely talented

00:12:37.791 --> 00:12:41.248
and wanted me to dance in
one of his music videos

00:12:41.248 --> 00:12:43.961
which I thought was odd.

00:12:43.961 --> 00:12:45.461
So when I met him,

00:12:46.725 --> 00:12:49.493
I saw this incredible human.

00:12:49.493 --> 00:12:52.613
I didn't know him as
Prince, this big star.

00:12:52.613 --> 00:12:54.901
I met him and I spent
a lot of time with him

00:12:54.901 --> 00:12:59.858
as an individual and I
learned so much about myself,

00:12:59.858 --> 00:13:02.399
and about, again, just
being even more vulnerable

00:13:02.399 --> 00:13:04.839
I think to, in order to grow as an artist

00:13:04.839 --> 00:13:09.006
you really have to have that
side of yourself be open.

00:13:09.944 --> 00:13:11.561
You can do anything you want

00:13:11.561 --> 00:13:14.953
even if you're being told negative things,

00:13:14.953 --> 00:13:19.060
just to stay strong and find motivation.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.812
I'm 5'2", I started when
I was 13, I'm black.

00:13:21.812 --> 00:13:24.778
There's so many things,
but I've made it happen.

00:13:24.778 --> 00:13:28.361
I'm very lucky to be
where I am but it's a,

00:13:30.072 --> 00:13:31.239
it's possible.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.269
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:38.269 --> 00:13:41.191
I made this video because
Tiger Lily asked me to.

00:13:41.191 --> 00:13:42.296
Also if you want to nominate someone

00:13:42.296 --> 00:13:43.987
for the next top 10 video,

00:13:43.987 --> 00:13:46.472
please check the description
for a link to a video

00:13:46.472 --> 00:13:47.900
where you can vote for people

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:49.781
and put in your suggestions as well.

00:13:49.781 --> 00:13:52.038
I'd love to know what did
you take from this video?

00:13:52.038 --> 00:13:55.010
What was the most important
lesson that you learned,

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:57.361
that blew your mind, that
you're going to immediately

00:13:57.361 --> 00:14:00.206
apply to your life or
your business somehow.

00:14:00.206 --> 00:14:01.912
Please leave it down the comments below.

00:14:01.912 --> 00:14:03.317
I'm super curious to find out.

00:14:03.317 --> 00:14:04.208
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:14:04.208 --> 00:14:07.732
to William and Tim from
Projectauthenticity.org.

00:14:07.732 --> 00:14:08.834
Thank you guys so much

00:14:08.834 --> 00:14:10.952
for picking up a copy of
my book Your One Word,

00:14:10.952 --> 00:14:13.321
taking a picture, making a blog post.

00:14:13.321 --> 00:14:14.478
I really appreciate the support

00:14:14.478 --> 00:14:16.188
and I'm glad you enjoyed the read.

00:14:16.188 --> 00:14:17.813
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:14:17.813 --> 00:14:19.148
I believe in you.

00:14:19.148 --> 00:14:21.157
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:21.157 --> 00:14:23.293
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:23.293 --> 00:14:25.710
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:14:32.174 --> 00:14:34.365
- I think there's no real way of preparing

00:14:34.365 --> 00:14:37.175
for something that seems scary.

00:14:37.175 --> 00:14:40.135
I think it's really
important for a young person

00:14:40.135 --> 00:14:41.552
to not set limits

00:14:43.689 --> 00:14:45.772
on what their dreams are.

00:14:46.779 --> 00:14:49.028
If they have something in their mind

00:14:49.028 --> 00:14:51.122
and they feel strongly about it,

00:14:51.122 --> 00:14:52.468
give it your all.

00:14:52.468 --> 00:14:54.604
Before I danced, I was extremely shy

00:14:54.604 --> 00:14:57.118
and I literally wouldn't speak.

00:14:57.118 --> 00:15:00.049
And I was terrified too
and my way of communicating

00:15:00.049 --> 00:15:02.441
started out by writing in journals.

00:15:02.441 --> 00:15:04.496
With the opportunity of
writing Life in Motion

00:15:04.496 --> 00:15:08.850
and Firebird, it's kind of
taken me to the next level.

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:10.916
And I'm just getting better and better

00:15:10.916 --> 00:15:14.074
about feeling confident about
how I communicate things.

00:15:14.074 --> 00:15:16.675
And it's extremely different writing

00:15:16.675 --> 00:15:19.066
but it all kind of ties
into the same thing.

00:15:19.066 --> 00:15:22.468
I think that this experience
has made me a better performer.

00:15:22.468 --> 00:15:25.092
It took a while to really find myself

00:15:25.092 --> 00:15:26.842
and to find the right

00:15:28.634 --> 00:15:30.314
way of taking care of your body.

00:15:30.314 --> 00:15:34.798
I'm sure every professional
dancer goes through that.

00:15:34.798 --> 00:15:37.848
Being a teenager to an
adult and your body changes

00:15:37.848 --> 00:15:42.201
and also, I think that, my
body type is very different

00:15:42.201 --> 00:15:43.644
from a lot of dancers that I dance with.

00:15:43.644 --> 00:15:44.616
- Absolutely

00:15:44.616 --> 00:15:48.607
- So like I was saying it just took me

00:15:48.607 --> 00:15:53.012
just accepting that I am beautiful
and that I have this body

00:15:53.012 --> 00:15:55.810
and just accepting me for me and I think

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:59.305
that's when I really found this confidence

00:15:59.305 --> 00:16:02.811
that I can go on stage and
I mean, Kevin the director,

00:16:02.811 --> 00:16:05.061
saw that as well and I think
that's when he promoted me

00:16:05.061 --> 00:16:06.281
and I think that's when I started

00:16:06.281 --> 00:16:08.531
getting more opportunities.

